    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's definitely harder to spot. i was also reading some older clinical notes about how pain management can be tricky depending on a patient's background. i've heard there's some debate about whether certain ethnic groups have higher thresholds for pain or if they just present differently. from a clinical standpoint, are there any documented differences in how different races experience or report pain that i should keep in mind for the boards?",
