      "content": "that makes sense, the systemic bias part is huge. but i was talking to an older attending resident, and he mentioned that in some practice settings, there's still a focus on biological differences—like how certain groups might have different physiological responses to opioids or different autonomic nervous system reactivity. even if it's controversial, does the literature suggest any specific racial or ethnic groups that tend to require different dosing or have different biological predispositions when it comes to pain sensitivity or analgesia? just trying to be as thorough as possible for the exam.",
